{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Arrow: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja13'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 13 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Sīlavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Ethics </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>3. Kaṇḍijātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Arrow: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Dhiratthu kaṇḍinaṁ sallaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Curse the dart, the arrow </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>purisaṁ gāḷhavedhinaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>that deeply strikes a man. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dhiratthu taṁ janapadaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Curse the nation </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yatthitthī pariṇāyikā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>where women rule. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Te cāpi dhikkitā sattā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Those creatures are cursed </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ye itthīnaṁ vasaṅgatā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who fall to women’s sway. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Kaṇḍijātakaṁ tatiyaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
